{title: This Is the Day}
{subtitle: Psalms 118:24}
{key: C}
{tempo: 119}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [C] | [C] | [F] | [G] | ×2
| [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]When the sun comes up and I [F]open my [C]eyes
[F]I can see the [C]morning in the [D]bright blue [G]sky
I [C]stretch up tall and I [F]jump out of [C]bed
[F]I re[C]member what the [G]Bible [C]said
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
This is the [F]day the [G]LORD has [C]made
Let us re[F]joice and be [G]glad in [C]it
This is the [F]day the [G]LORD has [Am]made
Let us re[F]joice [G]and be [C]glad in it
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Clap, clap, clap when the [F]sun is [C]high
[F]Stomp, stomp, [C]stomp when the [D]rain comes [G]by
[C]Turn around and [F]jump and [C]sing
[F]God has made each [C]day and [G]every[C]thing
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[F]Monday, [C]Tuesday, [G]Wednesday, [C]Thursday
[F]Friday, [C]Saturday, [D]Sunday [G]too
Give [F]thanks to the [C]LORD, for [G#dim]he is [Am]good
His [Dm]steadfast love en[G]dures forever
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]This is the [F]day the [G]LORD has [C]made
Let us re[F]joice and be [G]glad in [C]it
This is the [F]day the [G]LORD has [Am]made
Let us re[F]joice [G]and be [C]glad in it
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Re[F]joice and be [G][C]glad
Re[F]joice and be [G]glad in [C]it
{end_of_verse}
